      "Turn-flow example: 1. **Matching**: On your turn, you must match one end of a tile in your hand to an open end on the board. 2. **Drawing**: If you cannot play, you must draw tiles from the boneyard one at a time. For each tile drawn, you must pay 1 chip into the pool. 3. **The Auction**: When the boneyard is reduced to exactly **two tiles**, play freezes. An auction begins for those two tiles. 4. **Bidding**: Every player has a chance to bid twice (or check) in clockwise order. The highest bidder takes BOTH tiles into their hand and adds their bid to the pool. 5. **Ending**: A player wins by playing their last tile. If no one can play and the boneyard is empty, the game is 'Blocked'.",
